Bank loans: what they are, types, how to apply, requirements | Economy Finance
When the money does not come for something we want to buy, many times the solution that comes to mind is bank loans.
Are there various types?
1.1 What are the most important elements of bank loans
In other words, we are dealing with an interaction between the bank, which takes on the role of lender, and that of a person who needs that money, the borrower. Of course, to lend that amount of money, a series of interest rates must be applied, that is, some "extra earnings" for which it is profitable for these banks to lend that money.
Actually, the final objective of a loan is none other than to grant a certain amount of money to a person or company so that it can buy or pay for a certain service or purchase. However, the truth is that there may be several reasons that move that borrower to apply for these bank loans.
When applying for a bank loan, you must take into account the fundamental elements that you must understand perfectly. Namely:
Interest: is the price that the borrower will have to pay for lending the capital. It is extra money that is calculated in each loan by the banks.
Of studies. As its name indicates, they are the ones used to cover tuition and expenses generated in the studies.
In Spain there are many types of lenders that you can go to, but if we talk about bank loans, the main places are:
A clarification is that you can request a loan both in Spanish banks and also in foreign ones as long as they have representation in Spain.
Do you want to know what they are the requirements What are banks going to ask you for when you want a bank loan?
However, in general, there are some important requirements that must be taken into account and they are the following:
This is important, although if we take into account that the DNI can be obtained from the age of 14, the vast majority would meet this requirement. have solvency.
On the one hand, you have to guarantee regular income, that is, show that you are going to be able to repay the money that they are going to lend you. This does not mean that you should have everything, but enough to take care of the monthly installments that will make you pay.
It is the so-called guarantee of payment or endorsement. Some bank loans do not request it, especially when the amount to be lent is low, but in other cases they do.
If you are on that list or you have defaults, they will not grant you the loan, although in these cases you can go to private companies since some do not take this requirement into account.
Latest payroll or employment contract (to ensure you can return it).
Properties in your name.
Now that you know everything related to bank loans, it will be easier for you to identify the clauses, requirements and everything you need to know about them. Doubts?
