because this commonwealth it comes from afar and is closely related to the history of the United Kingdom itself.
Shortly after that date, in 1926, an Imperial Conference was held where it was declared that Britain and her dominions had equal status, but that all of them were united by loyalty to the Crown and that is why they were associated in a group, the Commonwealth.
But even so, many countries are part of this commonwealth, and even more have joined (and others, like Ireland, have disassociated).
This commonwealth has a Declaration of Principles that acts as a Constitution. It was signed in 1971 in Singapore and in 1991 it was ratified.
To maintain it, each country contributes an amount based on GDP and population.
You have to know that is made up of 54 countries around the world.
