After the food is put into the pot, water is not added first, but directly into the steam to heat up. Because there are cold spots in the air in the pot during the sterilization process, the heat distribution in this way is not the most uniform.
High temperature sterilization is very important for a food processing plant. It has the following two characteristics:
One-time: The high-temperature sterilization work must be completed at one time from the beginning to the end, without interruption, and the food cannot be sterilized repeatedly.
The abstraction of the sterilization effect: the sterilized food cannot be detected by the naked eye, and the bacterial culture test also takes a week, so it is impossible to test the sterilization effect of each sterilized batch of food.
