Who says sweatpants are only for lazy days lounging at home?
Of course, before you begin, you need to learn the lingo first. You’ve probably heard the words “joggers” and “sweatpants” used interchangeably, but are they really the same thing?
And does it matter what you call them, as long as you know how to wear them?
They’re generally loose-fitting (although some styles may be a bit tighter) and taper off to an elasticized ankle. Don’t confuse either style with “track pants,” which are usually longer, lighter weight, and loose around the ankles.
Are you pounding the pavement or hitting the gym?
Or will you simply wear them when you’re relaxing around the house?
Heavyweight sweatpants may be too much for a tropical climate, whereas lightweight joggers could be ideal. On the other hand, don’t buy thin joggers if you’re exercising outdoors in the dead of winter.
When you do it right, you can rock those sweatpants on a shopping day or a night out on the town. Here are a few sweatpants style tips for the ladies.
Dress Them Up with a Trendy Jacket
Rather than “sweating” from top to bottom, pair your sweatpants with a stylish coat, blazer, or jacket. A belted trenchcoat, navy blazer, or leather jacket could give your outfit the pizzazz it needs to stand out.
Add some style (and some height) with your favorite pair of heels, pumps or wedges. If it’s cold outside (or you prefer the look), pair those sweats with your favorite ankle boots instead.
A casual (but not overly casual) look works best with sweatpants.
Of course, if you’re working out, a tank top or muscle shirt looks great with our sweatpants. If you’re looking for a quality cotton t-shirt, check out No Love 4 for fitted styles and to support your preferred children’s charity.
Stick with a shirt that’s a solid color and avoid bright patterns. The same goes for your jacket, scarf, or other layers.
But if you’re hoping to dress up your sweats for another occasion, opt for a fitted black pair. They can’t quite replace those nice khakis or dress slacks, but if you do it right, they can come close.
Whether you’re hitting the pavement, lounging at home, or going out for a night on the town, there’s a function for every pair of sweatpants.
It’s time to find the perfect pair for you.
Do you have other questions or concerns before you make your purchase?
Firstly, you have to know that sportswear plays an essential role while working out in the fitness gym, and therefore should be chosen with care. Generally, cotton is the best fabric consisting of natural fibers, because it lets the skin breathe and absorbs sweat very well.
Secondly, depending on the activity that you perform you should adapt your outfit. For instance, if you are biking, long pants or leggings are not a good choice because they might cause you troubles like tripping or getting stuck in the pedals.
Mix a classic top portion of your outfit – thecrewnecksweatshirt and chambray shirt – with a very laid back bottom half.
