In this post, we’ll dive into joggers vs sweatpants to help you understand the difference. We’ll also throw in some styling tips for men and women so you can rock those pants on any occasion.
Classic sweatpants come in shades of gray, although you may find some in black or navy too. Joggers may come in a wider variety of colors and feature additional design details, such as a stripe down the outside of the leg.
When you’re shopping for sweatpants (or joggers), your purchase should depend on how you’ll wear them.
Do you intend to “dress up” your sweatpants and make a fashion statement?
The best sweatpants are made from 100% cotton for maximum comfort and breathability. The “weight” you choose depends on your climate and where you’ll be wearing them.
There’s nothing more comfortable than lounging in baggy sweatpants at home. But when you’re out and about, overly baggy pants can make you look sloppy.
Sweatshirts are cozy and comfortable, but they may not make the fashion statement you’re hoping for.
Another way to jazz up your sweatpants outfit is to leave the sneakers at home.
The right shoes are the easiest way to dress up your outfit and tie everything together.
How can men wear sweatpants in a stylish fashion?
Stick with a slim-fit T-shirt, as baggy pants and a baggy shirt will only make you look disheveled. Pairing your sweats with a simple polo or button-down shirt is a lesser-known fashion tip.
Your sweatpants are likely to be a solid, neutral color. Wearing a shirt that’s too “loud” will throw off your appearance—or make you look like a throwback from the 90s.
Many sweatpants come in gray, and that’s fine for casual wear.
The fabric’s weight is the main difference, and you can choose according to the climate you live in (and how you intend to use your pants).
Now that you know the difference between joggers vs sweatpants, what’s next?
