The costs for carrying on a business are those related to operations in sales. For example, your rent, phone bill, utilities, employees, marketing, little baggies for the above-described coke dealer, everything except the costs of the goods sold (COGS).
Costs of goods sold are those incurred in growing and preparing the crop for market, while those of carrying on the business are those related to its sale. As a result, cultivation centers have to worry about the double tax less than dispensaries.
