Very often the state granting the social equity certification sets their own requirements. In New Jersey social equity, the state requires the following;
Federal, State, or local government correspondence issued to the owner applicant which includes but is not limited to Social Security Administration documents, court issued notices, and property tax bills. Documents shall include the name of the owner applicant, address, and year(s).
State or Federal issued identification card that includes name of the owner applicant, address, and year(s).
Local, State or Federal Court records, Probation documents, Department of Corrections or Federal Bureau of Prisons documents. All documents must contain the name and date of birth of the owner applicant, date of the marijuana related offense and the date of conviction or offense.
