(1) How TFT works TFT is the abbreviation of “Thin Film Transistor”, generally refers to thin film liquid crystal displays, but actually refers to thin film transistors (matrix)-can be “active” to each independent on the screen The pixels are controlled, which is the origin of the so-called active matrix TFT (active matrix TFT). So how exactly is the image produced?
Everyone knows the three primary colors, so each pixel on the display screen needs three similar basic components described above to control the three colors of red, green and blue respectively. The most commonly used one is twisted nematic TFT LCD (Twisted Nematic TFT LCD).
The grooves on the upper layer are arranged longitudinally and the grooves on the lower layer are arranged horizontally. When no voltage is applied to the liquid crystal in its natural state, the light emitted from the light-emitting layer of the twisted nematic TFT display working principle diagram of Figure 2a will be twisted by 90 degrees after passing through the interlayer, so that it can be smoothly transmitted through the lower layer.
