ERAis a dice game by Matt Leacock for 1 to 4 players, ages 10+, and lasts 45 to 60 minutes. It is based on the idea of being successfulDice game through the agesand is the first "Roll & Build" game.
What immediately caught our eye and impressed us were the detailed miniatures of the buildings, which are a real eye-catcher for us to this day, every time ERA comes to the table during a game, we get the same feedback from our guests. What is also very appealing for casual gamers is that the set of rules is very simply explained and clear.
Finally the resources can be spent and buildings can be built, it should be noted that a city which is surrounded by a wall is then scored twice, this should never be ignored. Resources that are not spent this round are taken into the next.
As soon as there are no more buildings of 3 types of buildings, there are special tokens that are in the middle and then turned to x.
In itself a very nice game with a great replay value, but we have to admit that we were a bit disappointed with the board because you have to stick on all the number lines for the resources, culture and disaster points and the phases.
You should always keep in mind that Roll & Write, or in this case Roll & Build, is a pure game of chance and if you simply roll the dice badly, there is no chance of winning.
But as I said, all in all a very fun and beautiful game which can pave the way for a good start to a game night.
