Because here we have to expand our company, plant, dry, roast and deliver coffee beans. Sounds like a crazy business game to you ?
Well, not exactly, but it takes a lot of planning to get to your points.
To do this, we always have to cover parts of the old cards that are already on display with the new card,
! It is quite demanding to find the balance in your company between buying your own coffee, having enough action points in your trains and performing all your actions effectively, as it can happen that not enough drying fields or roasters are available.
We receive the points for delivering to our customers and there is also a final inventory assessment. We think the solo player mode in this game is more like an accessory, it means you can play solo, but it is more exciting or less fun, at least it felt like that to us.
It does not require a lot of material and is easy to get started with, even for young people.
However, this does not mean that café is an easy game, because if the right cards don't come up you have to improvise and think about your move for a long time.
Since everyone is playing more or less for himself, except when choosing the cards, you don't really have the impression of playing against each other, only when the final settlement of the points does it get serious.
For us, coffee was still a real game surprise in 2021.
NOTE: If all players already have a Level 3 Madness card, this consequence may not be chosen. In this case, the leader must roll the penalty die.
Should we have made it and reach the brink of madness, then we can now take flight. However, we always have to be aware of the more relics we carry with us on our way to the summit, the better our final rating will be.
Definitely a good mood game with us. Even if you have the ambition to want to win, you can't take the game wrong if you don't win.
In that sense, sometimes madness and genius go hand in hand.
