But what do we have for command cards ?
There are basically 4 types of cards in play, moving, exploring, building and training.
If we have no more cards in our display, we have to declare our shift over and put our discard pile back in our display. We remember when we finish our shift, the satellite always moves one space on the timeline.
When we have completed a module, we place a research tile on it and draw 2 cards from the incident pile.
What really makes this game so special is that the difficulty markers for the individual modules are randomly distributed in each game. The difficulty marker gives the total value in the skill building that you need to complete a module.
If there is a construction stop we cannot of course build on a module, but we can get a robonaut to help us who supports our actions with a plus 1 in each skill.
When we give the command, we take a training marker in any skill.
If for any reason we do not achieve our intermediate goals, the game will end prematurely.
