Catham is essentially a collect and discard game, at the beginning you put together the deck of cards from 5 of the 8 factions.
There are always 7 cards in the middle of the table.
Each of these factions can be collected and discarded in a different way, eg with the scientists you have to discard 3 scientists, for this the player receives 2 campaign points and 2 cards from the draw pile. Each faction has its own discard rules and the players trigger different effects each time.
Because you can put together the deck of cards with the 8 fractions differently for each game, there is a great variance.
