Basically the game is very simple, you put a planet sequence of 1 - 4 around the sun in the middle (the smartphone) in the best case of your own color and close it with a spaceship. The player who has completed it receives the finished stack.
In addition, all factions have special weapons (action cards) available such as planet destroyers, protective shields, tractor beams, combat squadrons.
Depending on the selection of the solar system, the game goes over several rounds and after the end of the last all points are added up.
For us, Lost Galaxy is a very dynamic but also exciting game that is influenced by random events and not least the players.
As always, we have impressive characters and powerful weapons at our disposal.
In addition, you can only use energy weapons on the planet's surface - projectile weapons are useless here. In addition, a very big innovation is "focus fire" with this attack option, you have the opportunity to defeat an abomination / monster or a fat / tank at the beginning, but this does not mean that the game has become easier.
We noticed that while you now have more opportunities to defeat your opponents, there are just as many to lose in this game.
The new player tablos appear tidy and well structured.
The new rules, the miniatures and the material are very good and immediately made me want more. The game has not gotten any easier because of the new advantages that you enjoy.
What has definitely disappeared is what I call the “warm up phase”. In the previous versions, there were only a few opponents in the zombie phase at the beginning and you could slowly start and collect equipment.
The price is like all Zombicide games in the upper range, but this is mainly due to the amount of miniatures that are included.
