In each round one player secretly writes a word on the blocks of all players - except for one. The player who doesn't know the word is the conspirator for this round.
Since each player has the opportunity to explain his choice of card in phase 4 and if the conspirator does this particularly well, he may not be exposed by the other players.
You have to think up a word that has to match two of your cards, because you have to lay both out in front of you.
Now each player receives a random block, which you must keep secret at all times.
Phase 3 “Play card” now each player has to display a card in front of him, which one
When all players have laid out a card in front of them, the active player lays down his second card for the word. It is important that the active player is the only one who puts the cards in the middle of the table;
In phase 4 “Discuss and vote” the active player announces the word, then all players have to explain why they chose these cards for this word.
Phase 5 "Scoring" here all blocks are turned over and the points are distributed.
If there is 0 or 1 magnifying glass next to the conspirator's tile, the conspirator receives 5 points and the active player 4.
The game ends (with 6-8 players) when everyone was one of the active players and (with fewer than 6 players) when each player was the active player twice.
The player with the most points wins.
