Water is already a precious commodity in our world, also in hydropower, where we try to generate as much energy as possible with our industrialized country.
But for that some work is necessary, like building dams, building pipe works and constructing turbine houses. Each country has 12 hardworking workers, which we place one after the other on our building board, the management plan and the patent office.
We use the power plant control to pump out water and thus generate energy.
The Bank action gives us 1 x Hydro for every worker that we place on it.
The Patent Office is an additional part of the map where you can purchase more advanced building technologies.
If we have uncovered a value with an exclamation mark through our construction campaign, we will receive this immediately and every round in the income phase.
A very interesting feature is the construction panel, because seen in this way you don't lose an excavator and concrete mixer, but get them back after the work is done. As I said, this process can be accelerated in the workshop.
The playing time is program and you should take a lot of time to plan your moves carefully.
In addition, the illustrations are a bit dark, but still very pretty and harmonious in the direction of steampunk.
For me, hydropower has already got a special place in our games cabinet on the one hand because it really feels different to play and is convincing with its original theme. On the other hand, because it has a solo mode, which I think is really very well done.
With this in mind, we hope you have a successful energy production and lead your nation to victory.
