In the travel phase we can now start collecting the dream fragments for our dreams.
In this case, our movement is free of charge; if there is no stone left on the key field, the movement is also free. In addition, once per round we are allowed to use the ability of a place on which our character (our shepherd) is written, for example “Draw 2 random dream fragments from the bag and place them anywhere”.
In the design phase we now start to recreate our dream by placing our dream splinters on the board according to our dream card, but we have to observe a few rules.
Each additional splinter must be placed next to a splinter or on an empty splinter (i.e. one with nothing on it).
The dream shards that you still hold in your hands at the end of the phase must be thrown back into the bag. It is often better to place them all in your Dreamscape, even if you do not need them there at the moment.
Splinters of water (blue) For a refreshing swim or an exciting dive. If your dreamer pulls over a splinter of water or stops on one, you immediately receive 1 snooze point.
Movement splinters (white) You can discard these heavenly splinters (see Discarding splinters on page 8) to move your dreamer. For each discarded white splinter, you move your dreamer to an adjacent splinter.
Whoever has the most dream points at the end wins.
However, we couldn't avoid giving Dreamscape our "top seal" because it really is a perfect game for us and the replay value is very important through changing dream cards and dream goals.
With this in mind, we wish you a wonderful dream trip without nightmares.
