Woods of Tarnaris - Path to Luslaria is a children's card game that combines mechanisms from “Memory” and “Ligretto” or “Skippo”. Each player has 20 cards with the numbers 1-10 face down twice and must try to discard them in front of the other players.
“I know!” You hear it from the right you hear it from the left and you have no chance of getting rid of your cards. Anyone who thinks Woods of Tarnaris is a very slow, quiet game is twisted wrongly because the opponents can quickly intervene and destroy their own move by playing their cards.
On a 5, the player may shuffle any 4 cards from another player.
On a 10 all players are allowed to look at a card from their deck and if the card fits, they can shout “I know”.
Due to the fast gameplay, Woods of Tarnaris is not a game for a quiet evening, but it should still be on the table, whether playing with the family or just playing a round of board games.
For us, Woods of Tarnaris is a very fun game that can be taken back again and again in board games, the rules are very easy and quick to learn, also perfect for in between thanks to the lean playing time.
