A PTO drive shaft is a method of transferring power from the engine and PTO to the onboard accessory equipment. The PTO drive shaft is used when there is not enough space next to the engine for additional accessories; the PTO shaft bridges the gap between the engine PTO and the accessories, allowing the accessories to be mounted elsewhere on the vehicle.
PTO drive shaft is a vital piece of equipment because it is responsible for creating a secure connection between various machines. There are many different types of PTO shafts, and you should find one that matches the specifications of your machinery.
U-joints are an essential part of a PTO drive shaft, and they must be the right size to avoid causing damage. A constant-velocity PTO shaft must maintain constant velocity in all directions in order to maximize the power transfer from the tractor to the attached implements.
You will see PTO shafts being used whenever equipment does not have its own engine. For example, you’ll often see a power take-off used in commercial vehicles and agricultural equipment.
Our PTO shafts are built to last, and we provide reliable service through durable construction. Our high-performance PTO drive shafts are the most important drive shaft solution for the agricultural, turf and lawn industry.
Check the minimum and maximum length of the drive shaft installed on the machine. In working conditions, the drive tubes should overlap 2/3 length and the plastic tubes should never be separated.
