The problems affecting the accuracy of the peristaltic pump are all caused by changes in the elasticity of the hose, there are three reasons for the change of hose elasticity:
For the same hose, if the gap between the roller and the arc is too small, or the gap is uneven, the hose will be partially over-extruded, resulting in plastic deformation, resulting in a dramatic change in the elasticity of the hose, thus affecting the transmission accuracy. Uneven pressure tubing can also lead to a significant reduction in hose life, increasing the cost of operating the peristaltic pump.
