Method for improving filling accuracy of peristaltic pump：
Use angle control technology to control filling volume. This method adds the angle control technology during shutdown on the basis of using the number of pulses to control the filling volume to ensure that the peristaltic pump rollers are in the same position every time the peristaltic pump is stopped, thus eliminating the impact of the peristaltic pump pulsation on the filling volume.
In general, peristaltic pumps use natural rubber hoses. The inner and outer layers are complete and smooth natural rubber, which is designed to be very resistant to abrasion.
It does not produce any blockage for the fluid transportation with high viscosity and impurities, the pump has a long service life, high lift and high pressure at the pump port. The first priority for designers and users of peristaltic pumps is their ability to deliver highly abrasive media.
