Mesh fabric is very elastic, because most of the tulle mesh fabric is made of polyester and other chemical fiber fabrics, and polyester also has good elasticity. Mesh fabric has good anti-wrinkle performance, and it is not easy to pilling after washing.
When choosing, you must clarify your design needs and choose the right kind of net yarn. As an unconventional fabric, net yarn has some tips for its production and application:
Most of the mesh is not resistant to high temperature, so try to use steam to smoke and iron the folds, or use the low temperature area to iron carefully, it is best to use a cloth.
In order to prevent the dislocation of the net yarn during cutting, it is best to use a roller cutter, and a cutting pad that can be automatically demobilized is placed on the lower pad.
Put a edging cloth on the outside of the needle position between the mesh and the feeding teeth to give more support to the mesh, which can prevent the thin mesh from getting stuck in the pinholes or being scratched by the feeding teeth.
The net yarn structure will not fall apart, which makes the clothing edges made of net yarn do not need to bother to close the edges, just keep the original cut edges of the net yarn to show a good air texture.
It is recommended to use a bead needle to smoothly fix the fabric that needs to be sewn before sewing, so as to prevent uneven sewing caused by the elasticity of the mesh.
