Glare caused by the sun can be a dangerous distraction in airport air traffic control towers. A clear, unobstructed view outside is essential for maintaining a safe operational environment.
Solar Solve is a UK based manufacturer and supplier of specialised shading systems, delivering high quality products and services to the air traffic management domain for private, commercial and military clients.
The highly specialised shade film reduces heat build-up from the sun by 65%, reducing air conditioning requirements and therefore saving energy, saving money and creating a more comfortable working environment.
Since entering the aviation market in the late 1990’s SOLASOLV® has developed into a global brand and can customise products according to the specific needs of clients. A measuring and installation service is also available where required.
Our products are not limited to ATC – we have been providing bespoke solutions to heat and glare problems caused by the sun in a wide variety of industries, worldwide, for more than 30 years, so no matter what industry you are in, Solar Solve are the experts:
We have supplied and installed electrically controlled and manually operated SOLASOLV Aviation System Sunscreens and Shades in civil and military airport Air Traffic Control Towers worldwide including:-
Solar Solve have been designing and manufacturing anti-glare roller screens since 1988. With over 17,900 installations in more than 106 countries worldwide, we offer experience and expertise in effective sun and glare solutions to minimise your risk.
Our aim is to develop strong relationships with our customers and our staff are appointed as much for their approach to customer relations as their technical ability.
We would be delighted to discuss how we can contribute to the success of your next project.
Improved visibility and safety − glare is reduced by up to 91% to ensure clear visibility and improve the controllers vision of both air and ground traffic and runway activity. True colour rendition is maintained so navigation lights, tail markings and other objects can be easily identified.
A comfortable working environment − keeps temperatures more uniform throughout the tower to ensure operators are alert and help maintain work-rate by rejecting up to 65% of the sun’s heat.
